    "kind": "Note",
    "title": "Cloud infrastructure · plain-English notes",
    "topic": "DevFest · Analyst",
    "body": "Virtual machines: each VM runs its own guest operating system. Useful when OS-level isolation or a specific runtime environment matters.\n\nContainers: package applications and dependencies while sharing a host kernel. Often lighter than VMs; actual startup and isolation depend on the workload and configuration.\n\nKubernetes / GKE: orchestrates container workloads, including scheduling and configured scaling. Scaling is not automatically driven by consumer traffic in every setup.\n\nCloud Run: managed compute for containerized applications and jobs. It reduces infrastructure management; startup latency, billing and execution behavior depend on service configuration. Avoid describing every request as instant or billed only by exact milliseconds.\n\nAnalyst exercise: compare deployment effort, scaling, isolation, operating cost and team skills for the same workload.",
