    "body": "LLM: a model that generates outputs from inputs. LLMs can also participate in tool use; “LLM = static text only” is too narrow.\n\nAgent: an application that combines a model with instructions, state and tools to carry out a workflow. Capability depends on permissions, integrations and design.\n\nMulti-agent system: multiple specialized agents coordinated around a task. Additional agents can add overhead and complexity; cooperation is not a guarantee of accuracy or autonomy.\n\nVertex AI: Google Cloud’s platform for developing, deploying and operating AI/ML models and applications. Study deployment, evaluation, governance and business context.\n\nRelated concepts: prompting; context engineering; tool calling; RAG; embeddings; MCP; validation.",
